// The rigiddynamics package (a working name; Jon names packages): the solver half of a
// Jolt-like rigid-body physics engine. A program reaches it with 'import rigiddynamics'
// (and 'import rigidcollide' for the shapes it is given), and gets a World of bodies,
// joints and queries that it steps at a fixed rate:
//
//   mut w = World.make();
//   imm ground = w.addShape(Shape.single(Prim.box(new Vec3(20., 1., 20.))));   // rigidcollide's
//   imm crate  = w.addShape(Shape.single(Prim.box(new Vec3(0.5, 0.5, 0.5))));
//   w.createBody(BodyDef.staticAt(ground, new Vec3(0., -1., 0.)));
//   mut def = BodyDef.dynamicAt(crate, new Vec3(0., 3., 0.));
//   def.material = PhysMaterial.ice();                                          // slips
//   imm id = w.createBody(def);
//   w.step(1. / 60.);                         // or w.advance(frameSeconds): fixed steps, Fiedler's way
//   imm xf = w.transformOf(id);               // place the mesh by it: a Rigid (position, rotation)
//   imm events = w.takeEvents();              // contacts added and removed, sensors, sleep and wake
//
// What it has:
//   Bodies        static, kinematic (driven by velocity or moveKinematic) and dynamic; mass and
//                 inertia from the shape and a density (or a mass), with a centre of mass off the
//                 shape's origin (compounds, off-centre hulls); linear and angular velocity, damping,
//                 gravity factor, forces, torques and impulses; layers and masks; sensors; a material
//                 each (friction sliding and static, restitution, rolling resistance).
//   Contacts      sequential impulses with accumulated, clamped impulses; warm starting from a
//                 persistent contact cache (points matched by position); a friction cone at the
//                 manifold's centre with two tangents, a twist row and rolling resistance;
//                 restitution above a speed threshold; Soft Step for position correction;
//                 speculative contacts from the narrow phase's margin.
//   Joints        point, fixed, hinge (limits, motor), slider (limits, motor), distance (rod, rope,
//                 spring) and cone-twist (swing cone or, with setSwingEllipse, an elliptical swing range of four
//                 quarter-axes; twist range). A point, hinge or cone-twist joint may also be
//                 DRIVEN (setJointDrive, setDriveTarget): its relative rotation held to a target by a spring of its
//                 own stiffness and damping in torque units, the torque capped, solved in the joint's own sweeps
//                 (a ragdoll's muscles; the ragdollrig package).
//   Sleeping      islands by union-find over contacts and joints; sleep after half a second of stillness;
//                 woken by contact with something awake, a joint, an impulse or a kinematic body.
//   CCD           a body that moves more than half its size in a step is swept (rigidcollide's shape
//                 cast) against static bodies, or against all if it is a 'bullet'. A body on a joint is swept
//                 only if it moves farther than the speculative contacts reach (maxSpeculative): putting it
//                 back would tear its joint open.
//   Character     a kinematic capsule (character.cone): slides along walls, climbs steps, refuses and
//                 slides down steep slopes, follows the ground down, stands on and is carried by moving
//                 bodies, pushes light ones, reports its ground.
//   Queries       ray cast, shape cast, overlap and point queries against every body, filtered by layer,
//                 with an excluded body and optional sensors (query.cone).
//   Events        contact added, persisted (if asked) and removed; sensor enter and exit; sleep and wake.
//
// Conventions: geomath's and rigidcollide's (right-handed, y up, metres, kilograms, seconds, f32). A body's
// id is its index in the world's table (a u32; slots are reused). A body's position is where its shape's
// origin is (World.transformOf); it is the centre of mass that the solver moves (World.centerOfMass).
// Shapes are registered once (World.addShape) and shared by every body that names them.
//
// Method choices (each a published algorithm, cited where it is coded):
//   integration         semi-implicit Euler, 4 sub-steps a step (Catto's Soft Step); the gyroscopic term
//                       solved implicitly with one Newton step (Catto, "Numerical Methods", GDC 2015)
//   contact solver      sequential impulses (Catto, GDC 2005 and 2006), warm started; friction after
//                       the normal rows; points swept forward and then back, contacts in graph-colour order
//   position correction Soft Step: soft constraints in implicit form, separation tracked through the
//                       sub-step, a relax pass without bias (Catto, Solver2D 2024; Box2D v3). Not
//                       Baumgarte (it adds energy) and not split impulse (it needs a second velocity set)
//   friction            Jolt's centre-of-manifold two-tangent cone with a twist row, Box2D v3's rolling
//                       resistance; Coulomb with a static and a dynamic coefficient
//   restitution         Newton's law at the end of the step, over a speed threshold (Box2D v3)
//   speculative contact Catto, "Continuous Collision", GDC 2013 (the margin grows with speed, to a limit)
//   joints              Jolt's and Box2D's rows (see joint.cone), soft in Soft Step's way, with the spring taken on
//                       the heavier body's mass (PhysX's joint inverse-mass scale idea: a foot's joint must hold
//                       the body above it) and swept settings.jointIterations (8) times a sub-step together with
//                       the contacts of jointed bodies, so a push from a contact crosses a chain of joints in a
//                       sub-step, not a link a sub-step. The elliptical swing limit is Jolt's SwingTwist idea
//                       with four quarter-axes.
//   sleeping            islands by union-find; Box2D's speed measure (speed, or spin times radius)
//   broad phase         rigidcollide's sweep and prune, behind its BroadPhase trait (see below)
//   continuous          Box2D v3's sweep to the time of impact, body put back and left to the contacts
//   character           collide and slide (Fauerby 2003) as Jolt's CharacterVirtual
//   graph colouring     greedy, dynamic-against-dynamic contacts first, contacts against static last
//
// What is not here (yet): a second broad phase (spatialindex's dynamic BVH would replace sweep and prune
// at tens of thousands of bodies; the World holds a SweepAndPrune), threads or SIMD (the colours are
// computed and the solve is in colour order, so that is a swap and not a rewrite), a six-degree-of-freedom
// joint, joint breaking, soft bodies, stale-id detection (ids are indices, not generation-tagged), rotation
// in a shape cast, a world save and restore, a character that is also a rigid body, and a determinism proof
// across machines (one run is deterministic bit for bit: pairs are sorted, nothing iterates a hash map; no
// float is combined in an order that depends on a thread).
//
//   common.cone      constants, PhysMaterial, Settings, Event, Softness, small maths
//   body.cone        BodyDef, Body
//   contact.cone     the contact cache and the contact solver
//   manifolds.cone   tidying the narrow phase's manifolds for meshes and heightfields
//   joint.cone       joints and their rows, the angular drive
//   world.cone       the World: bodies, joints, the step, the broad phase, sleeping, CCD
//   query.cone       ray, shape and overlap queries, QueryFilter
//   character.cone   the character controller

mod rigiddynamics;

import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import rigidcollide use *;
